// CotSC Batch 18 - extracted original English dialogue for carnival.d
// Keep existing @ numbers stable when translating.
@1 = ~Enjoy your stay at the Carnival.~
@2 = ~Enjoy your stay at the Carnival.~
@3 = ~Enjoy your stay at the Carnival.~
@4 = ~Enjoy your stay at the Carnival.~
@5 = ~Enjoy your stay at the Carnival.~
@6 = ~What a lovely fair.~
@7 = ~Me like this place. It be more nice than orc lands.~
@8 = ~This is genuinely the most wondrous fair I have ever been at. I came all the way from Gullykin to see it. It's truly fabulous.~
@9 = ~By Helm! This wasn't the statue. What kind of a deprived monster would turn a living person into a stone.~
@10 = ~Look at the level of details. The pose, facial expression, the attention to detail. I would love to have a statue like that in my manor in Waterdeep.~
@11 = ~In that case I wish you luck. Show him the taste of your steel! Here, take this, my dear woman. You'll need all the help you can get.~
@12 = ~The deprived monster's name is Tranzig, and the title you just gave him harmonizes well with his nature. He will pay with his life for this once I find him.~
@13 = ~If you want to watch me breathe fire, make some space.~
@14 = ~Ooh, I wanna see it! Hey, do you think my hair would catch fire if I tried that? Let me try!~
@15 = ~Ehm... no. Do NOT try that. I mean it, Imoen.~
@16 = ~If you want to suffer excruciating pain, be my guest.~
@17 = ~I'm only kidding. What do you think the trick is? A potion? A spell? Must be magic, right? Magic is so beautiful.~
@18 = ~Pah. You'd burn yourself and, knowing your clumsiness, everything else around you. Stick to picking locks and stealing bananas like a monkey, which fits your personality well.~
@19 = ~Tell me, fire-breathing friend, how does one acquire such a glorious burp of righteousness? If Minsc could breathe the flames of justice, the eyes of evil would melt like butter on a hot summer stone! Boo thinks it is a matter of diet, perhaps extra spicy nuts?~
@20 = ~A true master never reveals his secrets.~
@21 = ~Ooh, wow! Look at that! It's so big and bright and pretty! *Squee!* You're like a human dragon, but way nicer and not trying to eat us! Everyone look, look how high the sparklies go!~
@22 = ~By the icy breath of Auril! In the frozen wastes, we use fire to keep the death-chill at bay. But you? You weaponise it for the glory of the crowd!~
@23 = ~Being a wild mage sometimes makes me forget how many tricks ordinary people can hide up their sleeves. It looks impressive enough, for a party trick, of course.~
@24 = ~Nothing but a party trick. I could show off real fire at your beck and call.~
@25 = ~If you want to watch me breathe fire, make some space.~
@26 = ~Tell me, fire-breathing friend, how does one acquire such a glorious burp of righteousness? If Minsc could breathe the flames of justice, the eyes of evil would melt like butter on a hot summer stone! Boo thinks it is a matter of diet, perhaps extra spicy nuts?~
@27 = ~A true master never reveals his secrets.~
@28 = ~Ooh, wow! Look at that! It's so big and bright and pretty! *Squee!* You're like a human dragon, but way nicer and not trying to eat us! Everyone look, look how high the sparklies go!~
@29 = ~By the icy breath of Auril! In the frozen wastes, we use fire to keep the death-chill at bay. But you? You weaponise it for the glory of the crowd!~
@30 = ~Being a wild mage sometimes makes me forget how many tricks ordinary people can hide up their sleeves. It looks impressive enough, for a party trick, of course.~
@31 = ~Nothing but a party trick. I could show off real fire at your beck and call.~
@32 = ~you approach a friendly wolf who sits on the ground and watches you with curious eyes. He appears to be guarding the tent. You can pet him if you wish. Maybe he won't bite your hand off. Maybe…~
@33 = ~1) (Pet the wolf)~
@34 = ~2) (Leave him)~
@35 = ~you scratch wolf behind his ears, and it seems like he likes that. He lets out a satisfied bark and lies on the ground~
@36 = ~I see vexation growing in these peasants when I collect all their money. I won most bets so far.~
@37 = ~I'm definitely out of luck. I lost all the money I bet. But I want more. I... I can get it back.~
